=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported fault does not exist in the network. Exhaustive probing from laptop0 (172.16.20.10/24 — the only device on the 172.16.20.x segment) to every host in the 172.16.10.x segment yielded 0% packet loss on all five targets: the inter-VLAN gateway at 172.16.10.1 (router0.eth0.10, TTL=64), PC4 at 172.16.10.4 (TTL=63), PC5 at 172.16.10.5 (TTL=63), laptop2 at 172.16.10.12 (TTL=63), and laptop3 at 172.16.10.13 (TTL=63).

The inter-VLAN design is working correctly: switch1 places 172.16.10.x hosts (pc4, pc5, laptop2, laptop3) on br_vlan10 and the single 172.16.20.x host (laptop0) on br_vlan20; mswitch1 trunks both VLANs upstream to router0; router0 terminates VLAN 10 on eth0.10 (172.16.10.1/24) and VLAN 20 on eth0.20 (172.16.20.1/24) with ip_forward enabled and no iptables rules whatsoever. ARP tables on both laptop0 and router0 are populated and correct. The return path from 172.16.10.x to 172.16.20.x is equally healthy — pc4's default gateway (172.16.10.1) resolves to the same router0 interface.

Root cause: there is no fault; the network between 172.16.20.x and 172.16.10.x is fully operational.

Corrective action: no network change is needed. The user's perception of a connectivity loss may have been transient (e.g., a brief ARP resolution delay at startup) or a misidentification of the affected device. The helpdesk should verify the user's local host settings (correct gateway 172.16.20.1 assigned, no local firewall) and confirm the issue is no longer reproducible.
=== END ===